OL,3,CRough sleeping up by 23% according to
OL,4,Clatest figures
OL,6,FThe number of people rough sleeping in
OL,7,FWales was up by 23% this May, when
OL,8,Fcompared to the figures for May 2025.
OL,10,FNew figures released by Welsh
OL,11,FGovernment show an increase from 131
OL,12,Findividuals sleeping rough, to 162.
OL,13,FThat is the highest figure recorded
OL,14,Ffor May over the past three years.
OL,16,FThe local authority that recorded the
OL,17,Fhighest number of rough sleepers was
OL,18,FCardiff at 45. Then at second but
OL,19,Fsignificantly less was Swansea with 18
OL,20,Findividuals, followed by Pembrokeshire
OL,21,Fat 15.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G1/6
