OL,3,CRough sleeping up by 23% according to
OL,4,Clatest figures
OL,6,FMore than 10,000 homeless people were
OL,7,Fbeing housed in temporary
OL,8,Faccommodation in May 2025 - down from
OL,9,Fthe previous month and when compared
OL,10,Fto last year.
OL,12,FA quarter of those people (2,505) were
OL,13,Fhoused in bed and breakfasts and
OL,14,Fhotels, making that the most common
OL,15,Ftype of temporary accommodation.
OL,16,FCouncil owned properties housed 2,457
OL,17,Fhomeless individuals.
OL,1,Wj5hw}j5 ~shws                   G2/6
OL,2,W+.-'*%/"-$+,(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
